  "live_records": {
    "q-37007": {
      "dom_id": "step-q37007",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "What is the range of the function $h$ defined by the following table?\n\n| $x$ | $-5$ | $-\\frac{2}{5}$ | $0$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $3$ | $4$ | $\\frac{9}{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $h(x)$ | $\\frac{9}{2}$ | $4$ | $3$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-\\frac{2}{5}$ | $-5$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The range of $f(x)$ consists of all the outputs that have a corresponding $x$-input.\n\nIn a table, the range consists of all numbers that feature in the row corresponding to $h(x).$\n\nTherefore, the range is the set $\\{-5,-\\frac{2}{5},0,1,\\frac{3}{2},3,4,\\frac{9}{2}\\}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
