    "q-79267": {
      "dom_id": "step-q79267",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "What is the range of the function $h$ defined by the following table?\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $3$ | $-4$ | $5$ | $-6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $h(x)$ | $-7$ | $6$ | $-5$ | $4$ | $-3$ | $6$ | $-1$ | $0$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The range of $h(x)$ consists of all the outputs that have a corresponding $x$-input.\n\nIn a table, the range consists of all numbers that feature in the row corresponding to $h(x).$\n\nTherefore, the range is the set $\\{-7,-5,-3,-1,0,4,6\\}.$",
